<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIAN STOCKS SEEN WEAKER ON WALL ST DECLINE.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIAN STOCKS SEEN WEAKER ON WALL ST DECLINE.</headline>
<text>
<p>------------------(Snapshot 8.35 a.m./2235 GMT)----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	    2650.5   -16.7   DJIA cl	7960.84  -101.27</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl     2627.0   -22.0   US 30yr cl	6.68    +0.04</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.195  -0.010   Gold NY 324.80 Lon fix 326.10</p>
<p>AUD   US$0.7404  (Tue  $0.7394)   CRB Index cl  243.09    -0.66</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	19099.11 +274.93   FTSE cl	 5075.8    +43.9</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   926.60   -1.05   NZSE40	 2474.75   -23.33</p>
<p>--------------------------(Aug 13)-----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen weaker at open in line with offshore. &quot;With New York down and the commodities down you would have to call it lower,&quot; said Reynolds and Co dealer Peter Struk.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$17.01 (-.01), A$19.06 (-.04), A$5.88 (unch), A$7.40 (-.02).</p>
<p>*Wall Street weakened on interest rate jitters. The Dow industrials tumbled 101 points to close below 8,000.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 17-1/26 (-1/16), BHP 25-7/16 (unch), WMC 22 (-1/8), National Australia Bank 71 (-3/8)</p>
<p>*Base metals finished mostly lower although copper and aluminium staged late rallies. Gold weakened on moderate volumes while oil strengthened.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
